 228:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h **** /**
 229:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @param channel Constant pointer to USIC channel handle of type @ref XMC_USIC_CH_t \n
 230:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 				  \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC0_CH0, @ref XMC_USIC0_CH1 to @ref XMC_USIC2_CH1 based on device sup
 231:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @param config Constant pointer to UART configuration structure of type @ref XMC_UART_CH_CONFIG_t
 232:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @return XMC_UART_CH_STATUS_t Status of initializing the USIC channel for UART protocol.\n
 233:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *          \b Range: @ref XMC_UART_CH_STATUS_OK if initialization is successful.\n
 234:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *                    @ref XMC_UART_CH_STATUS_ERROR if configuration of baudrate failed.
 235:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *
 236:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * \par<b>Description</b><br>
 237:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Initializes the USIC channel for UART protocol.\n\n
 238:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * During the initialization, USIC channel is enabled, baudrate is configured with the defined over
 239:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * in the intialization structure. If the oversampling value is set to 0 in the structure, the defa
 240:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * is considered. Sampling point for each symbol is configured at the half of sampling period. Symb
 241:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * majority decision among 3 samples. 
 242:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Word length is configured with the number of data bits. If the value of \a frame_length is 0, th
 243:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * is set to the same value as word length. If \a frame_length is greater than 0, it is set as the 
 244:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Parity mode is set to the value configured for \a parity_mode.
 245:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * The USIC channel should be set to UART mode by calling the XMC_UART_CH_Start() API after the ini
 246:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *
 247:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
