 287:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h **** 
 288:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h **** /**
 289:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @param channel Constant pointer to USIC channel handle of type @ref XMC_USIC_CH_t \n
 290:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 				   \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC0_CH0, @ref XMC_USIC0_CH1 to @ref XMC_USIC2_CH1 based on device su
 291:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @param rate Desired baudrate. \n
 292:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *           \b Range: minimum value = 100, maximum value depends on the peripheral clock frequency
 293:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 				   and \a oversampling. Maximum baudrate can be derived using the formula: (fperiph * 1023)/
 294:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @param  oversampling Required oversampling. The value indicates the number of time quanta for on
 295:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 					 This can be related to the number of samples for each logic state of the data signal.\n
 296:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 					 \b Range: 4 to 32. Value should be chosen based on the protocol used.
 297:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * @return XMC_UART_CH_STATUS_t Status indicating the baudrate configuration.\n
 298:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 			     \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC_CH_STATUS_OK if baudrate is successfully configured,
 299:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * 					 @ref XMC_USIC_CH_STATUS_ERROR if desired baudrate or oversampling is invalid.
 300:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *
 301:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
 302:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Sets the bus speed in bits per second.\n\n
 303:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Derives the values of \a STEP and PDIV to arrive at the optimum realistic speed possible.
 304:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * \a oversampling is the number of samples to be taken for each symbol of UART protocol.
 305:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * Default \a oversampling of 16 is considered if the input \a oversampling is less than 4. It is r
 306:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * a minimum oversampling of 4 for UART.
 307:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  *
 308:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_uart.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
